  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cry of the Excluded</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Cry of the Excluded is a continental network present in 23 countries. It works around the general themes of integration, migration, debt, trade and militarization, as well as around the specific themes that arise from each country&apos;s context. The continental headquarter is in Brazil. 

This project is part of the Economic Justice Programme, a partnership between CAFOD and 4 church-based organisations, whose goal is to achieve greater economic justice in Brazil by addressing the key development issues of debt, trade, governance and human rights with a focus on awareness-raising, participation, social mobilisation and advocacy.

The project seeks to: (1) bring about an increased social inclusion by: a) publicizing the Economic Justice Programme&apos;s theme &quot;debt and social rights&quot;; b) raising the awareness of the excluded in the Americas about their rights; c) strengthening the 12 October (in the Americas) and 7 September (in Brazil) as dates that symbolize the resistance and fight of the excluded; (2) promote the resistance, in every country where it works, to the social and economic models that keep the majority of the population excluded; (3) promote more transparency of the governments in relation to how they manage their debts; (4) strengthen the Economic Justice Programme partnership; (5) strengthen the Programme&apos;s work methodology at an international level.</narrative>
  </description>
